# The preload: the standard language every program gets, as whole definitions with their bodies (notes/wap.md
# "Layers"). A built-in is declared here like any function; its body is a primitive, `prim`, where warp ends and wasm
# or the host begins (notes/kernel.md "Primitives"). The compiler knows none of these names: the declare stage reads
# their signatures from this file, the emitter their bodies.

# a text written to the standard output, then a line end
print(t: text) := prim print_text(t)
